Title: THE VOICE OF ONE
Credit: Written by Dale Joseph
Author: Dale Joseph
Source: from the Voice of One canon
Draft date: 2026-08-18
Contact: The Emergence Institute

====

FADE IN:

INT. SITUATION ROOM - DAY

No sound first.

Screens stacked in a room with too much glass. On every one:

A Black man on pavement. A knee on his neck. Uniforms around him like a ritual circle. A phone camera shaking not from hands but from the person breathing behind it.

CARMICHAEL watches on mute. Always mute first.

He exhales through his nose.

AIDE freezes the frame. The man's face tilted enough to see the whites of his eyes.

Beat.

CARMICHAEL
Run it again. With sound this time.

Sound floods — begging, orders, phone cameras, the high keening of people watching a man die and knowing nobody in uniform cared.

When it ends, nobody speaks.

ATTORNEY GENERAL
It's bad.

CARMICHAEL
No. It's disastrous.

He folds his hands on his stomach.

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
Walk me through liability.

The AG starts: procedure, exposure, unions nervous but will stand down if contracts untouched.

COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR
We can condemn the act without
condemning the institution. Bad apples,
retraining, independent review —

CARMICHAEL
And the base.

COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR
They're watching. They want to know if
you're still their man. If you go too
hard on the cops, they hear it as you
choosing them over us.

Silence. Carmichael stands. Walks to the window. Lawn immaculate beyond gates. He turns back.

CARMICHAEL
Here's what we're not going to do. We
are not going to throw the entire law
enforcement community under the bus to
satisfy a mob that will hate me again
by next week.

Relief moves around the table.

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
We'll say it's tragic. Demands review.
Independent. Transparent. We'll show
faces of reform.

He lets that sit. Then, level:

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
Mute out. Sound up. Crowd in.

Phones already moving. A staffer cues the edit — crowd sound fills, mute lifts elsewhere on another feed.

CARMICHAEL
We curate which stories count as the
country.

No one argues. He does not raise his voice.

CUT TO:

EXT. RALLY FIELD - DAY — MONTHS LATER

Heat. Flags snapping. Crowd as weather.

CARMICHAEL at the podium, mid-sentence, sleeve tugged by wind.

A crack — not loud enough at first to be a gun.

The crowd ducks as one body. Carmichael tips, hand to ear — red on fingers.

Screams. Suits cover him. He is pulled down behind the podium, then through a curtain.

INT. ARMORED CAR - DAY — CONTINUOUS

Doors shut. Engine already moving.

Carmichael's hands shaking. He holds them together so the agents won't see.

CARMICHAEL
Are we clear?

LEAD AGENT
For now. Shooter's in custody. Local PD
is securing.

CARMICHAEL
Any word on casualties?

The agents exchange a look.

LEAD AGENT
Two confirmed injured, one critical.
We'll have more soon.

Carmichael closes his eyes.

He knows what he is supposed to think. He thinks: They missed.

He sees it: wind, angle, his own head turning a fraction of an inch to check the teleprompter. He should have been dead. He is not.

He focuses on that. Not the blood. Just the fact: I am still here.

INT. SECURE LOCATION - EXAM ROOM - NIGHT

Fluorescent. Doctor fussing. No bullet wound — a graze along the ear, a line of blood that looks dramatic on camera and trivial on the chart.

DOCTOR
You're very lucky.

CARMICHAEL
(nods)
Thank you.

INT. RESIDENCE - NIGHT — LATER

Carmichael alone. A drink he doesn't need. A Bible he hasn't opened in years on the side table.

He picks it up. Flips it like a deck of cards, pages slapping against his thumb until it falls open somewhere in the prophets.

His eyes land on a word.

CLOSE ON PAGE: ANOINTED.

He stares at it. Knows what it is — a translation dragged across centuries.

He seizes it anyway.

CARMICHAEL
(soft, to himself)
Anointed.

Beat. He knows the physics — wind, angle, jittery trigger finger would have been enough. He does not need the physics.

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
If God did not want me here, that
bullet would have finished the job.

No thunder. No vision. A cheap lamp, dust, old coffee smell still on his sleeve from the exam room. He closes the book. Does not pray. Places it back squared to the table edge.

CUT TO:

INT. WAR ROOM - NIGHT — WEEKS LATER

Maps. Numbers narrowing on a screen. Paper cups.

CAMPAIGN MANAGER on speakerphone. Tired.

CAMPAIGN MANAGER (V.O.)
Key suburbs underperforming. Turnout
shifts in the cities. The path is
very narrow. We need to prepare a
statement.

CARMICHAEL
Narrow isn't closed.

CAMPAIGN MANAGER (V.O.)
No, sir. Not yet. But the networks will
probably call it within the hour. We
need to prepare a concession —

CARMICHAEL
No.

Beat. The room stills.

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
No concession.

COMMUNICATIONS DIRECTOR
Sir, if we concede we defend the count —

CARMICHAEL
The margins tell me what was counted.
Not what was cast.

He steps closer to the speakerphone.

CARMICHAEL (CONT'D)
Do you believe the people who chanted
my name in the rain, who drove six
hours to stand in a field for three —
just changed their mind because a few
pundits called me dangerous?

The line is quiet.

CAMPAIGN MANAGER (V.O.)
Public opinion can —

CARMICHAEL
Public opinion is a product. Someone
else has outbid us.

He hangs up before they can answer. Looks at the table.

A staffer has a graphic open: LOST. Cursor blinks.

Carmichael reaches past him. Takes the keyboard. Deletes LOST. Types himself, hunt-and-peck:

STOLEN.

Second staffer duplicates the map. Drags the second forward. No one argues arithmetic.

CUT TO:

INT. HALLWAY - PRESS EDGE - DAY

Fluorescent, same building as the file rooms. No podium — a hallway with worse acoustics.

SANDI, AIDE at her elbow, tablet ready.

AIDE
(quiet)
They're shopping it. The photo. Brooklyn.
Inbox to inbox. Not yet posted. Waiting
to see if you blink.

SANDI
How far.

AIDE
Two forwards.

SANDI's face shortens. Harder, not dramatic.

SANDI
She's focused on her health and her
future.

The pronoun held.

AIDE
Window's closing. They want 'our.'

SANDI
They'll wait. Send exactly that. No
'our.'

The AIDE notes it verbatim. Then, lowering voice, phone buzzes:

AIDE
You were off the four o'clock. They
moved it without you — secure briefing.
I wasn't told to tell you.

SANDI hears it. Doesn't break stride. Nods once.

SANDI
Note the time you told me.

AIDE
12:43.

SANDI
Thank you.

She walks on toward the briefing room. Tries her badge at the door — light stays red. She does not try twice.

Through glass: the briefing already underway inside, seats taken, a chair where she would have sat now holding a stack of folders.

She turns away. The cost is a closed door, not a stride.

CUT TO:

INT. ONE'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

ONE alone. Pen. Radio low. No laptop — paper.

He writes. Reads aloud to the empty room, testing weight.

ONE
(reading, tired authority)
'Publish precinct evidence. Preserve
records. Permit independent review.'

He stops. Adds, plain:

ONE (CONT'D)
'An unverified claim will not become a
stage.'

He reads it once more to the empty kitchen. Folds it. Photographs it plain, background blank, text-only.

He posts the addendum. Comments disabled, as before.

INSERT — SCREEN: the post, white background. No face.

CUT TO:

INT. WHITE HOUSE - PRIVATE STUDY - NIGHT

The same room. Now an AIDE reads the addendum aloud from a printout. Flat. No spin.

AIDE
'Publish precinct evidence. Preserve
records. Permit independent review. An
unverified claim will not become a
stage.'

CARMICHAEL listens, still. The AIDE finishes.

Silence. Then:

CARMICHAEL
Get me the continuities.

AIDE
Sir —

CARMICHAEL
Not the usual staff. The other meeting.

The AIDE understands. Exits with the paper.

Carmichael alone, the addendum on his desk, the muted stills still underneath, the narrow maps still narrow.

No words about causation. He picks up the handset.

CUT TO:

INT. CONFERENCE ROOM - NIGHT

Not the Situation Room. Smaller. Chairs that don't match — borrowed prestige.

Not the usual staff. TECHNOCRATS. Lanyards, not lapel pins.

A memo on each chair: FEASIBILITY REVIEW (RESTRICTED)

Carmichael at the head, but not performing.

TECHNOCRAT
(small, procedural voice)
This is not an authorization. This is a
feasibility review — whether guidance
can be made continuous across absence.

No one says whose absence. No name is written.

TECHNOCRAT (CONT'D)
If asked, we would look at what would be
required. Not what has been done.

Forms. Initials. A box checked: REVIEW. Another box, unticked, reads AUTHORIZE — left empty on camera.

Carmichael does not raise his voice. He initials the margin where the form requires it.

CARMICHAEL
Feasibility only. Report back on what
would be required — not what you have
done.

The forms are collected. No one claps.

FADE OUT.
